From: Kelvin Jiang <kelvinjiang@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:33:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] [Extensions] Validate context and target event in
 events.*Rules

Original change's description:
> [Extensions] Validate context and target event in events.*Rules
>
> Restrict the internal `events` feature entry in `_api_features.json` to
> `privileged_extension` contexts so `events.addRules`, `events.getRules`,
> and `events.removeRules` cannot be invoked from content scripts or other
> non-privileged contexts.
>
> Harden `RulesFunction::Run()` and
> `RulesRegistryService::GetRulesRegistry()`:
> 1. Require a non-null `Extension*`, `kPrivilegedExtension` context, and
>    non-negative `web_view_instance_id` before mutating or parsing
>    `args()`.
> 2. Replace prefix matching in `GetDeclarativeAPIType()` with an exact
>    allowlist of the three rule-supporting events
>    (`declarativeContent.onPageChanged`,
>    `declarativeWebRequest.onRequest`, and
>    `webViewInternal.declarativeWebRequest.onRequest`), enforce
>    `(web_view_instance_id > 0) == (api_type == kWebRequestWebview)`,
>    and reject frameless, Service Worker, or non-`webview`-permissioned
>    `<webview>` calls.
> 3. Check `ExtensionAPI::IsAvailable()` on `event_name` (returning a
>    normal error when an optional permission has been revoked or the
>    rules registry is unavailable) and defer `RecordUMA()` until after
>    validation and registry lookup.
> 4. Replace the debug-only `DCHECK_EQ` in
>    `RulesRegistryService::GetRulesRegistry()` with a runtime check.
>
